      "side": 1,
      "message": "`sanitized_path` is consumed as a C-string in two places:\n* `format()` on line #517 that builds `path`.\n* `content_type_from_request()` on line #564, which resolves the file extension via `hash_get_mem()`. That table is built with `hash_create_string()`, so lookups go through `strlen()` on the key.\n\nSo, even with `%v` on line #517, `content_type_from_request()` would still `strlen()` past the non NULL terminated vector into the ASan redzone whenever a real file with an extension is served. `vec_terminate_c_string()` terminates the vector once at the source and covers both cases.",
